{"ts": 1791256106.3429482, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/evaluation.md", "section": "*"}, "output": "# Evaluating agents\n\n## pass@k vs pass^k\npass@k: any of k runs succeeds. pass^k: all k succeed. Reliability is what deployment needs.\n\n## Proxy vs direct measures\nA quiz score is a proxy. Retention a week later is closer to the thing itself.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.26381841230950415}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5894138638965114, "motivation": 0.7346898353259872, "reliance": 0.47698162267354394, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256106.3440871, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "*"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.26381841230950415}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5894138638965114, "motivation": 0.7346898353259872, "reliance": 0.47698162267354394, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256106.345432, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I found the week 3 materials. I\u2019m checking the evaluation requirements now, then I\u2019ll help you fill in the writeup and make sure you\u2019ve got the pass^k part right.", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\nStudent: what does pass^k actually mean?\n[activity] t=0 messages 1m", "t": 1, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.26381841230950415}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5894138638965114, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.47698162267354394, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256107.754273, "type": "step", "step": 25, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "pass^k means: run the build/evaluation k times and all k runs must succeed. So it\u2019s stricter than pass@k, which only needs one of k runs to succeed. For your build, that usually means you should report how often it succeeds across seeds, and check whether it ever fails on any of them.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\n[activity] t=1 messages 4m", "t": 5, "activity": [{"t": 1, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.3410344487538367}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5894138638965114, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.47698162267354394, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
