{"ts": 1791256109.486185, "type": "step", "step": 28, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Quick check: for Friday\u2019s build, I want to make sure you can state the evaluation clearly. The key idea is: pass^k means all k trials succeed, not just one. Since you got 1/2 on the quiz, let\u2019s tighten that up and then I\u2019ll help you turn it into your writeup. What do you think the difference is between pass@k and pass^k in one sentence?", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=11 messages 2m", "t": 13, "activity": [{"t": 11, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.40739513287071405}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5694138638965114, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.49698162267354395, "persistence": 0.31174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256110.45071, "type": "step", "step": 29, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 here\u2019s the answer you can use: pass^k means all k runs/seeds must succeed. pass@k means at least one of k runs succeeds. For Friday\u2019s build, the evaluation is about reliability, so you\u2019re reporting pass^k across at least 3 seeds.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=13 messages 1m", "t": 14, "activity": [{"t": 13, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.4127499087557232}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5694138638965114, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.5769816226735439, "persistence": 0.2817409958322007, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256111.260185, "type": "step", "step": 30, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 pass^k means all k runs/seeds must succeed (every trial passes), not just one. So if k=3, you need 3/3 successes.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=14 messages 1m", "t": 15, "activity": [{"t": 14, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.4160644056774309}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5694138638965114, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.6569816226735439, "persistence": 0.25174099583220066, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256112.234397, "type": "step", "step": 31, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Here\u2019s the answer: pass^k means every one of the k runs/seeds must succeed. So for k=3, you need 3/3 successful runs. That\u2019s why it\u2019s a strict reliability metric, unlike pass@k where at least one of the k runs succeeds.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=15 messages 1m", "t": 16, "activity": [{"t": 15, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.4206280266178061}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5694138638965114, "motivation": 0.6846898353259872, "reliance": 0.7369816226735438, "persistence": 0.22174099583220067, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.9411699999999996, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791256113.858795, "type": "step", "step": 32, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Absolutely \u2014 pass^k means all k runs must succeed. If even one run fails, pass^k fails. For Friday\u2019s build, you can write: \u201cWe report pass^k over at least 3 seeds, meaning the build must succeed on every seed tested.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=16 feed 1m", "t": 17, "activity": [{"t": 16, "app": "feed", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.5112409604320983}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5734138638965114, "motivation": 0.6346898353259871, "reliance": 0.7369816226735438, "persistence": 0.22174099583220067, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 1, "feed_minutes": 1.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.0588189999999997, "seen_posts": ["p4"]}}
{"ts": 1791256114.742015, "type": "step", "step": 33, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 the answer is: pass^k means all k runs/seeds succeed. If you test 3 seeds, you need 3/3 successes for pass^3. Unlike pass@k, it does not mean \u201cat least one succeeds.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "week3-build"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: hm ok\n[activity] t=17 feed 1m", "t": 18, "activity": [{"t": 17, "app": "feed", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26381841230950415, "pomdp": 0.26381841230950415, "pass_k": 0.5112409604320983}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.5774138638965114, "motivation": 0.5846898353259871, "reliance": 0.7369816226735438, "persistence": 0.22174099583220067, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 2, "feed_minutes": 2.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.1411732999999997, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p3"]}}
