{"ts": 1791256117.0098, "type": "step", "step": 38, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "Agent environments"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 38, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.26350112931521363, "pomdp": 0.26350112931521363, "pass_k": 0.5106261130402509}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7324138638965114, "motivation": 0.5862208517933883, "reliance": 0.7369816226735438, "persistence": 0.22174099583220067, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.31279709056453686, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2824851109524564, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 12.0, "phone_minutes": 5.0, "nag": 1.5705866499999999, "seen_posts": ["p4", "p3", "p6", "p5"]}}
